From: nikaminow <345005485+nikaminow@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: cancel self-refresh work on kms uninit

dpu_crtc_init() calls drm_self_refresh_helper_init() for every CRTC, but
nothing ever calls drm_self_refresh_helper_cleanup(). After an unbind the
delayed entry work can still run on the freed device:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000300
  Workqueue: events drm_self_refresh_helper_entry_work
  pc : drm_atomic_commit_alloc+0x18/0x98
  lr : drm_self_refresh_helper_entry_work+0x64/0x1f8

Seen on the Nothing Phone (3a) (milos), where the display is rebound once
at boot. Cancel the work and free the helper data while the CRTCs still
exist.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_mode_config.h>
+#include <drm/drm_self_refresh_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_vblank.h>
 #include <drm/clients/drm_client_setup.h>
 
@@ -231,10 +232,15 @@
 	struct msm_drm_private *priv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct drm_device *ddev = priv->dev;
 	struct msm_kms *kms = priv->kms;
+	struct drm_crtc *crtc;
 	int i;
 
 	BUG_ON(!kms);
 
+	/* DPU arms self-refresh entry work per CRTC: cancel it before the CRTCs go away */
+	drm_for_each_crtc(crtc, ddev)
+		drm_self_refresh_helper_cleanup(crtc);
+
 	/* We must cancel and cleanup any pending vblank enable/disable
 	 * work before msm_irq_uninstall() to avoid work re-enabling an
 	 * irq after uninstall has disabled it.
